    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a concentrated focus on attacking favorable matchups against Martinez and Feltner. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlines our starting unit with a 74.56 efficiency score, buoyed by a prime batting order slot and a significant platoon advantage against Feltner\u2019s 4.98 xERA. Close behind is **Drake Baldwin**, whose placement at the top of the order (10% boost) combined with the soft matchup against Martinez pushes him into the high-60s. While **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci** face a tougher test against Jones (3.57 xERA), their elevated batting order positions maintain their utility status, though they fall into the marginal tier as they navigate a pitcher who suppresses xwOBA better than our other opponents tonight.\n\nOur bench decisions were straightforward today, largely dictated by the light schedule for our core stars like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson**, all of whom are off tonight. **Dominic Smith** was the closest call for the final UTIL spot; his 58.04 score fell just shy of the \"Strong\" threshold but provided the highest floor among our remaining options. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains on the shelf, leaving a void in our stolen base production that we are currently monitoring through depth options like **Nasim Nunez** and **Wade Meckler**. We are keeping a close watch on weather reports for the night slate, but otherwise, we are prioritizing the high-upside deployment of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Drake Baldwin** to keep our Roto standing afloat while the rest of the roster rests.",
